# The GPU driver blocklist (docs/phases/phase-5.md item 5.17c).
#
# It ships with the release, embedded in the GPU process at build time. It is
# never updated remotely, and nothing is reported to any server. It starts empty:
# an entry is added only when a real failure is recorded, with a link to the
# evidence. The format is in crates/clazel-gpu/src/blocklist.rs; in short, one
# entry per line, fields separated by spaces, the reason last:
#
#   <api> <vendor> <device> <drivers> <evidence> <reason>
#
#   api       vulkan, d3d12 or metal
#   vendor    the PCI vendor id, 0x and 1 to 8 hex digits
#   device    the PCI device id, the same, or * for every device of the vendor
#   drivers   * for every version, or first-last, or one version; a version is 1
#             to 4 decimal parts of 0 to 65535 separated by dots; missing parts
#             of the first version are 0 and of the last 65535, so 470-470.57
#             covers 470.0.0.0 to 470.57.65535.65535
#   evidence  an https:// link to the recorded failure
#   reason    the rest of the line: what goes wrong
#
# For example (not an entry):
#   vulkan 0x10de 0x2204 470-470.57 https://example.org/issue hangs on the first frame
